  "scope": "Continue shared boxing mechanics: coherent lead/rear stance through physical body/guard/punch/support, and continuity of the contact-to-return arm pose.",
  "authority": [
    "docs/boxing-foundations/START_HERE.md",
    "docs/boxing-foundations/True_North_Boxing_Foundation.md: mirrored stance, coordinated body chain, foot support, continuous transitions and authoritative contact",
    "docs/boxing-foundations/Boxing_Styles.md: learned technical methods remain independent of broad archetypes",
    "User camera correction: behind and above player, opponent facing screen; no gameplay camera changes in this correction."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Mirror ordinary and learned stance blade, foot stagger, longitudinal weight bias and lead-hand guard through shared stance roles. Anatomical punch inputs remain left/right.",
    "Lead-straight loading follows the actual lead hand; body dip transfers toward the actual lead foot. Existing authored punch timing, damage and other character values are unchanged.",
    "Resolve equal foot-placement errors and equal step-opening directions by stance role, avoiding arbitrary right-foot selection and the resulting opposite-leg loading after an angle change.",
    "Preserve the existing constrained elbow plane when stopping a glove at contact. The old authored arm pole preceded the final body/IK solve and could introduce unrelated elbow displacement.",
    "Add native comparisons for body disk, high guard, all ten head/body punch families for both actors, supported movement in six directions, three guarded combination/exit sequences and exact in-flight save/restore."
  ],
  "fixture_boundary": "Mirror comparison explicitly exchanges authored left/right punch tuning as well as stance and input so physical reflection is compared at equal timing/effort. It does not change live game tuning or claim distinct characters should fight identically. Captured gameplay retains actual authored tuning.",
